chapter-54.md He sat across from Cael and ate his barley steadily and slowly, as he ate it every morning, and when he had finished he set his spoon down in the bowl and folded his big hands on the wood.
chapter-54.md He had thought he would not be able to, but his body had decided otherwise without consulting him, as it had on every morning before every floor since he was twelve.
chapter-54.md Under the table, against his knee, he folded down one finger of his left hand, as Brom made a mark in his number column, and kept it folded.
chapter-55.md He came through the rope with his feet a shoulder-width apart, as he walked everywhere, and stood in the chalk square as if he had been asked to hold up one end of the room.
