chapter-55.md And the Warden stood beside his cases and let it lie, as he had let everything lie, and Lira understood for the first time why Cael had stopped being angry at him.
chapter-56.md Naveth walked back to the academy's table, upright and slow, as he always walked.
chapter-56.md He felt the whole length of it, as he had once felt the half-second at the Ironyard before Reydan's name went up on the board beside his own.
chapter-57.md Cael felt her there, as she had said he would.
