editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:129:**Defect — chronology at the ch43/ch44 join (introduced by the repair).** ch43 now ends with Karis catching Cael "at the foot of the worn stair after the others had gone" (the new charter beat). ch44 then opens: "Nobody left the provost's office after that; they stayed another hour with the challenge squared on the blotter and divided the three weeks up between them". The reader has just been told everyone left. ch44's breakup paragraph then has "the six of them came apart in five directions … Karis went toward the residence wing … Cael stood alone … and watched the five of them go", which contradicts Karis having lingered, and her "two steps up the passage toward the archive". Pre-repair ch43 ended on "Thank me if it works." and ch44 opened on the division; the inserted beat is in the wrong place. Fix: move Karis's beat to ch44 after the breakup paragraph, with that paragraph's Karis clause and "five directions" removed (exact strings in §5). The beat itself is good and should be kept whole.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:139:**Checked and clean.** No fragment, dangling referent or speaker separated from a line in any changed region. Every cross-reference into a rebuilt scene still has its referent: Karis's "since the scarred table on Monday night" and "On Monday, in the stable, from what you told us. *Exposes its own charter to review.*" (ch42 has Cael give them "the charter" and Coss's line is "exposes its own charter to review"); "A week ago I told a whole room I'd keep you a fighter" and "I said he would be. In the provost's office" (ch44 s1 has both); "the small box he had drawn on the night of the council" (ch44 log, Wednesday night); "the first draft in its leaning hand" (ch45); "Today proves you're real" and "The assessments that matter come later" (ch7); the Fenmark "nineteen words" (ch24, 26, 34); "A market interview … in the square" beside the Ardenmere "borrowed office" (both exist in the edition: ch6, ch13, ch39). The aide on the landing bench, then on the landing, then at the booth: consistent. The "two days in a borrowed office" / "a paper you'd found in two days": consistent.
