editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:43:- Protected wording inside this movement: P15 (definitions clause, ch45) verbatim; P17's language inside Quenna's D6 record (ch46) verbatim; §9.2 lines "New opponent. Four hundred pages, no tells, no third exchange." (ch44), "You were fourteen." … "This is also the job." (ch42), "After that, the job is to be right." (ch42), Prynn's sixty-years line (ch45), "'Warden' was never a town title" (ch42); Wray's D1 line quoted by Wray (ch43) verbatim. P3 is echoed, not quoted, by Lira and Quenna — correctly, since neither answers it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:44:- Reserved truths: no mechanism in any record; Coss never learns it and the aide only hears the rumor; the fourth file's eleven words stay unquoted and point nowhere; no "before Arbiters," no date on the rename, no assay clause, no Vastin, no Seln; the Level 4 remains a ruled bar; Tide untouched. Karis's founding-shelf report ("Ash and Stone and Current… nobody like you yet") stays on the right side of the UNBOUND plant.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:45:- Ember limits match BOOK_MAP §8.3 and the P1 notice: contact-adjacent (a hair, not a finger), single channel (it "picks"), one point, invisible cost shown to the reader first. Karis gives exactly one rewording ("a spark") and twice refuses a second; the "decision point" is not landed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:47:- Crowd of "three hundred" at the match (ch42, ch46) matches M5 ch36. Edran entering with a shell and an edge already up (ch45) matches M3 ch18. Fourteen rings on the post by week 19 is arithmetically exact. Wray's seven, six and twelve words are exact counts of her three record lines.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:48:- The "every amendment is a confession" plant: the manuscript gives it to the taxonomy master and makes him Prynn's former reader. M1's *prose* (ch5, line 43) has the soft-voiced taxonomy instructor say it; the M1 ledger entry (§3, "Registry-history instructor… her lines include 'Every amendment to a code is a confession'") is the one that is wrong. Ruling: the manuscript is right; the ledger line should be corrected, not the chapter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:49:- Reader Standard (Gate 27): `ed.sh gates` reports reader_standard=0, metadata=0, modern=0 on all seven files; my read agrees. No oaths, no gore (scorched boots, a bruise, grey fingertips), no innuendo. Brom's "I don't love him. I study him." / "That's how it starts." is affection teased, not romance, and passes; I note it only because it is the single line a cautious owner might look at twice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:52:1. **Coss's calendar cannot reach the gate (ch41, lines 541–599; canon: BOOK_MAP §3 "19 — Coss at the gate").** The regional registry enters Oona's line "eight days later" than the Tuesday of week 18, i.e. the Wednesday of week 19; Coss reads it that day, requests in-person service that night, is approved "by the middle of the next morning," is assigned an aide "the next morning," and sets out "before dawn on the Tuesday" to reach the academy "on the Monday following." Yet he is at Greyvane's gate on the Monday of week 19 (ch42, line 609), before any of that could have happened. Oona Kindled on the Saturday of week 17 and her sheet left on the Monday post; no reading of "eight days" puts the line in his hands before the Tuesday of week 18, and a six-day road from that Tuesday lands him on Monday week 19 only if he read the line by the Sunday before — impossible. This is a verified continuity contradiction, not plan adherence. Related, lesser: "He had been at the regional office nineteen days" (line 547) sits oddly beside the M2 ledger ("Coss is on the road to the regional office," week 5–6); ten weeks are unaccounted for. That one is an apparent inconsistency for the planner, not a contradiction.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:53:2. **Oona's age at her Kindling (ch41, line 435).** "a thirteen-year-old girl who had been afraid for seven weeks and two days." UNIVERSE_BIBLE: "At age 14, every person undergoes Kindling"; BOOK_MAP §5.5.1: "The child's Kindling arrives at fourteen in week 17"; M1 ledger: "Oona Kindles 'in winter' at fourteen." She is fourteen on the bench. One word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:55:4. **Soft lean on dating (ch45, line 1321).** Cael to Prynn: "a few hundred years of everybody treating it as if it were in the schedule." BOOK_MAP §10 forbids a date on the rename; this is not the rename, and "a few" is vague, but Book 6 dates the flag's existence to about two centuries. "Generations" would carry no risk. Optional.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:58:7. **New canon to confirm (all acceptable on the evidence):** Oona as Anchor Path, Copper (Anchor is on M1's hardening family chart and among the eleven Paths watched — an existing name, as the packet required); the charter rule admitting the Compact's officer of record to a pending respondent's assessment "as an observer, without voice" (nothing in canon forbids it; it is the cheapest way to make Book 4's thin exhibit true); Coss lodging over the draper's shop; the taxonomy master as Prynn's former reader (see above — consistent with M1 prose); Brom raised "on an estate where people were told what they'd seen."
