editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:61:1. **Coss's arrival date cannot be reached from the registry section (41 → 42).** Oona is assessed on the Saturday of week 17. The notation sheet goes up "on the Monday post" (week 18). The registry section opens "eight days later" immediately after the Tuesday-of-week-18 paper session; read from there, the line is entered on the Wednesday of week 19, two days after Coss is already at the gate (42: "the Monday of the nineteenth week"). Read from Oona's Saturday instead, it is entered on a Sunday, and Coss still needs: a request "that night," approval "by the middle of the next morning," an aide "the next morning," departure "before dawn on the Tuesday," and six days to "reach the academy on the Monday following." No anchoring of "eight days later" closes that chain onto Monday of week 19. The rest of the movement's day-count (Wednesday council = day 1; Tuesday of week 20 = day 7; Friday = day 10; hearing in week 22) is internally consistent, so this is a single joint, not a systemic drift.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:62:2. **Oona's age at Kindling.** 41: "a thirteen-year-old girl who had been afraid for seven weeks and two days." Elsewhere the text sets Kindling at fourteen (41: "their children came to fourteen on the road"; 42: "You were fourteen"; 41 digests: "a youth past the age of Kindling"). May be deliberate (assessment in the fourteenth year), but a reader will notice. Low-to-medium confidence that it is an error.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:64:4. **Which post (46).** The sitting uses "the oak post in its iron foot" fetched from section four. The spark post in the quiet room stands "in an iron bucket of sand" and by 44 carries seventeen rings. A reader briefly wonders whether Cael is burning the reading-post; one clause ("a clean post," or Hobb fetching "the quiet room's post") settles it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:65:5. **Repeated exposition (41 and 45).** The demonstration provision's origin ("written as a kindness... carters and drovers and pedlars") is narrated in full twice. Deliberate echo; the second instance could be cut to its new content (Cael's recognition that it was written for Oona) without loss.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:75:- Observed issue: the sequence (Oona's Saturday assessment → Monday post → registry entry → Coss's request, approval, credential, aide → departure "before dawn on the Tuesday" → six-day journey) cannot deliver Coss to Greyvane's gate on Monday of week 19 under any reading of "eight days later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:77:- Proposed scope: one of two small fixes. (a) Keep the Monday-of-week-19 arrival and compress the chain: anchor the registry entry to Oona's Saturday explicitly ("Three days after the girl came back up the hill..."), approve and depart within two days, and shorten the journey ("the coach to the hill town and the road up from there" is two days, not six). (b) Keep the chain as written and move the arrival to the Monday of week 20, shifting the handful of later week labels by one (42 "nineteenth"; 44 log "week nineteen"; 45 "Tuesday of the twentieth week"; 46 log "Twentieth week"; the hearing notice "twenty-second"; Lira's "twenty weeks"). Either is a paragraph's work. Do not touch the day-count from the Wednesday council onward; it is sound.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:84:- Proposed scope: delete one of the two "no scars" sentences; decide Oona's age and make 41 agree with the Kindling-at-fourteen rule or make the rule say "the year they turn fourteen"; add a clause marking the sitting's post as a different post; recast the Lira sentence ("...and walked him to the stable, and he ate a breakfast he did not want"). Four line edits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:87:**Priority 3 — Let someone name the counter the text has already given Coss (43 council, or 45 Prynn exchange).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:88:- Location: 42, Coss: "a chartered academy that keeps an enrollment it knows to be invalid puts its charter up for review"; 43, Cael's "The whole challenge assumes the Compact has authority over me in the first place"; 45, Prynn: "That's the clever answer... I asked for the true one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:89:- Observed issue: Cael's seam argues that the Compact has no authority over an unclassified person. But Coss's stated lever in 42 is not Cael; it is Greyvane's charter, which the Compact plainly governs. Four careful readers (Cael, Prynn, Naveth, Karis) all accept the seam across two chapters, and none of them says the obvious thing: the Compact need not touch him at all, only the academy that holds him. An adult genre reader sees this by the end of 43 and spends 44–46 waiting for the text to see it too.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:91:- Proposed scope: one short exchange, not a new scene. Best home is Naveth in 43 after "the academy won't stand in it" ("He doesn't need authority over you. He has it over me."), or Prynn in 45 after "That's the clever answer," with Cael boxing the line as *not yet*. Two to four sentences. Do not resolve it here; let the hearing carry it.
