editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:11:He knew that other thing. It was what fear became in him when it had been given long enough and something to push against. It had happened in Ardenmere with Reydan's name on the circuit board, and it had happened at the first sitting with Hobb across the chalk. A hearing was a formal proceeding, and formal proceedings ran on rules. Rules were written down somewhere. And anything that was written down could be read, closely and patiently, the way he had read every fighter who had ever tried to beat him, until he could see how it moved.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:15:Prynn was where he had left her that morning, at the high desk on her stool with her ledger open and her spectacles on their cord. She looked up as he came through the iron-banded door with the expression of somebody who had guessed from the runner's face hours ago that whatever it was would not be small, and had been waiting since then to find out how large.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:25:Prynn looked at him for a long moment with the same territorial care she gave to everything, the look of a keeper deciding whether a request would be worth the trouble of whatever shelves it disturbed. Then she nodded, once, as if he had already asked the question rather than only arrived carrying it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:35:It was a case. It went from the floor to the ceiling and was as deep as Prynn's arm was long. In it the bound volumes of the Compact's registry code stood in their dark identical spines, row on row, with the amendments filed beside them in thin paper fascicles tied with tape. Decades on decades of the same official language were laid down there like silt in a river bed, each layer pressed flat by the weight of everything that had been enacted since. The spines said what they were in faded gilt. *Charter. Schedule of Recognized Paths and Standings. Obligations of Practitioners. Enforcement.* He read the words and knew them for the inside of every room he had ever lived in, and knew too that he had never once seen them in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:39:"It's long," said Prynn beside him, watching him take its measure. "It's dry as anything on these shelves, and drier than most. It contradicts itself in four places I've found, and I've never had anybody to tell." She lifted the lamp a little. "And if you want my opinion, which you haven't asked, I don't believe a single person who enforces it has read it whole in my lifetime. They read the part that lets them do the thing they came to do."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:55:Prynn did not lock the door either night. He did not mention it, and neither did she. On the first night she came down off her stool at the eighth bell and put a cup of tea at his elbow and went back up, and on the second she did not come down at all, and the cup was there anyway when he looked up from the page, though he had not heard her bring it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:77:Oona was waiting for him outside the stable on the Tuesday evening, between the two nights, with her slate under her arm and a new tag on the string round her neck.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:79:He saw it before he saw her face. The hollow circle was gone, and in its place hung the academy's ordinary crest, a tower above a road, the same tag Brom wore, cut from the same tin by the same clerk. She had polished it. It caught the light from the stable door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:99:Oona considered this with her whole face, as she considered everything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:109:"I asked Gerda. She knows procedure." Oona turned to go, and then turned back. "She said it isn't unfair. She said it's procedure. I said I'd decide for myself."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:113:Wray stopped him at the rail of the defensive floor early the next morning, on his way to the provost's stair, with her slate on her hip and her brown coat buttoned to the throat. She did not waste anything on a greeting.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:119:"Seven words at the first. Six at the second. Twelve at the third." She looked at him with her level measuring eyes. "You counted them. Brom told me. I counted them too, when I wrote them. I chose every one." She tapped the slate once with a finger. "I want you to know that I'll stand by every word of all of them, if anybody asks me to stand. *Unorthodox architecture. Consistent execution. No safety concerns.* I wrote that about a boy I'd watched for a quarter of an hour, and I'd write it again about the one I've watched for a term."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:121:He did not know what to say. Wray did not seem to need him to say anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:125:"Whatever you do in that room," she said, "do it the way you fought Edran. Find what it's proudest of, and go there." She went back to her chalk, and called *Again* to somebody, and did not look back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:129:Naveth's office held six people only if all six agreed not to mind, and on the Wednesday morning, the third since the gate, the six people in it all knew before anybody spoke that nobody was going to be let off minding today.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:131:Two more chairs had been carried up the worn stair from somewhere, and set against the shelf of thin brown alumni books, and still Brom had to stand. Cael sat between Lira and Karis, on the side of the desk where people sit to be talked about rather than to talk, until Quenna, at the tall window with her arms folded, turned round and put that right without asking anybody's leave.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:135:Naveth did not object. He looked like a man who had spent the night arguing against himself and losing every round of it before the breakfast bell. He laid the challenge on his blotter and squared it to the edge, as a man squares a document he has read so many times he no longer needs the words. Then he said the thing that had plainly been sitting in his chest since Monday.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:141:"I want to be exact about what I mean," Naveth went on, "because I think it matters that all six of us are looking at the same problem and not at the comfortable versions of it. The enrollment, as we categorized it, is against the plain words of the provision's own gloss. Everybody in this room has known that since the afternoon we signed him in." He did not look at Cael as he said it, which was a courtesy. "The gloss says a candidate who has not yet undergone formal Kindling assessment. Cael has undergone it. The category was never his shape. We cut it to fit him because otherwise he'd have had nowhere at all, and I'd sign that form again tomorrow. But being willing to sign it again and being able to defend it in front of a magistrate are two quite different things. My counsel has spent two days confirming that there is no defence of the enrollment itself that survives a competent challenge. And the Warden's challenge is competent." He laid his long hand flat on it. "It may be the most competent document that has ever crossed this desk."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:143:He let that stand, and Cael watched the sentence cost him. Naveth had spent a long career being right about people other institutions were wrong about. Everything he believed about his work rested on the faith that a careful academy could shelter the mispriced inside honest paperwork. And here on his blotter, in the system's own words, was the demonstration that such shelter could only bear so much, and that he had gone on building after he knew it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:149:Naveth did not answer at once. Watching him pick his words, Cael understood that the provost was about to say aloud a thing he loathed, because it needed saying.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:151:"The least damaging option open to this academy," said Naveth, "is a negotiated withdrawal. We go to the Compact before the hearing. We concede the category error. We revise Cael's standing to whatever the provision's words actually cover, which, honestly, is nothing at all. He would leave us, under no category whatever. Greyvane keeps its charter. And the two hundred others in this building keep their places, every one of them, in smaller ways, a mistake the registry was made to find and value too cheaply." He looked at the blotter. "No other road keeps so many people so safe, so surely."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:155:"You're not recommending it," said Quenna. It was not a question.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:157:"No." For the first time since Cael had known him, Naveth looked plainly, honestly tired. "I won't be the man who kept that option off this table by not saying it out loud. It's real, and if I pretended otherwise I'd be telling a lie, and that is one kind I've never told at this desk. But I'm not going to recommend handing over a student to save an institution either. If that costs the institution in the end, I'd rather have made my peace with it before than after." He looked at Cael directly then, over his spectacles. "This is your enrollment, not mine to trade. So tell me what you want."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:161:He had walked the running road first. There was always running. There had been running every day since Denvash, and it went where it had always gone: somewhere smaller, with the same file arriving a season after him. He had walked the road Naveth had just set out so honestly that it hurt to hear, and found at the end of it a boy on a coach with a bag, and a provost writing a letter to a guild family about why the observer track was closed. And he had walked a third road, built out of two nights of lamplight and a word that carried a whole roof on its back, and of the three it was the only one he could picture putting in the binder without his hand flinching.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:171:Brom's eyebrows went up slowly, as they always did, a step at a time. Karis's pen, which had been lying still beside her notebook, was in her hand before she seemed to know she had picked it up. Naveth's counsel-trained caution began, visibly, to draft objections behind his eyes. But it was Quenna that Cael watched, because Quenna was the one who had staked her name on him in front of a panel of three. Nothing on her face moved. What moved was in her shoulders, a sudden tightening, the thing he had seen fighters do in the instant a bout turned into one they had not trained for.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:181:"It is different," said Quenna, "because if you're wrong, what you lose isn't a bout. It's everything the bouts were ever for."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:185:Brom, who had not said anything yet, made a small sound against the bookshelf that in another room might have been a laugh.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:189:Naveth looked at Cael for a long moment. It was the measuring look, the look of a man recalculating a wager he had already placed once and was now being asked, under fire, to place again. Whatever the sum came to, it came to the same answer as the first time. That was the whole of who Naveth was, Cael thought: a man who had built an academy out of doubling the bets other people folded.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-43.md:195:"Don't thank me yet," said Naveth. "Thank me if it works."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:5:POV is Cael's, close third, except for one cutaway: Coss, at the end of ch41, about 1,890 words (the regional office, the packet, Oona's notation line, the decision to file in person). The calendar runs from the Tuesday of week 17 to the last night of week 20.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:11:| 40 | Contact Only | 4,917 | Lira's five terms at breakfast. Contact only, one point, on something that isn't anybody, buckets; Karis adds that she will write nothing. Brom's post comes from the cook's woodpile ("She calls it kindling"). **First deliberate Ember test** in the quiet room at the sixth bell, by the first-encounter rule: intention stated aloud; palm on oak; no gathering and no glow, one instant; an ordinary small flame in the wood that keeps burning until it is sanded; bigger than asked. The cost comes after: a cold drop under the breastbone, cold down the arm, grey fingertips, and the warmth gone for about a hundred count. Lira saw nothing on his face. Karis: "That isn't my point… It doesn't behave like fire at all." Second try with the size chosen first; contact-adjacent tested (a finger's width, nothing; a hair, yes). **Karis's first rewording:** "You haven't got fire. You've got a spark… everything after the spark belongs to whatever you struck it on." Wed: five marks (Lira's limit, three). Thu: three of three at a thumbnail; Karis says *consistent, observable* aloud once. Quenna: "You're pale." Not doing it with nobody pushing proves nothing (boxed). Friday: Oona's mother arrives; "My mother on the left. You on the right." |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:12:| 41 | The Bench | 6,010 | Lira takes the top of the hill. The grey station: soap smell, the bench, and Denvash returning in his body. Oona's mother: "You're the one with the strange kind." Hands on both shoulders, taken away as she stands. Denvash let through all the way, from the bench to the road. **Oona: Anchor Path, Copper.** "It's ordinary." She holds her card unshown. The category's true user walks out of it, and the observer roll will hold one name. "Are you sorry?" / "A little… mostly I'm glad." Lira: "Ordinary's the best kind." Wk18 Tue: two-at-once always gives one ("it picks"), so **single channel**; through paper, the paper burns and not the wood; Karis keeps the scrap and has no second word yet. **Coss cutaway:** nineteen days at the regional office; the drafting records (the provision written as a kindness for travelling guild families' untested children); three precedents, none survived; Oona's notation line as the perfect exhibit of the provision's purpose; filing in person ("I don't need to"); the ruled bar again; the credential; the aide; the letter to his daughter. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:13:| 42 | Correct Papers | 4,871 | Monday wk19. The clerk and the seal; Coss crosses the yard. Prynn: "Whatever it is, the shelves will still be here." The walk, counting; the machine never breaks doors. Naveth's open door; Quenna's look, *say little, hear everything*. The card: "'Warden' was never a town title"; the file held since the week of his Kindling. The challenge: the gloss, the Denvash entry, the drafting records, the charter's exposure; filed in the room; Quenna's forty years answered, "*inventive* enough"; three weeks; "I have never seen it survive." At the door: "You were fourteen… This is also the job." Stair: "After that, the job is to be right." Competence used kindly. The family told: Lira (stay angry at the machine), Karis (a war fought with paper), Brom (the paperwork ought to be more worried). The draper's window: Coss in "the mothers' room". |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:14:| 43 | The Case at the Back | 4,679 | The notice text (hearing set for the first day of week 22, first bell, assembly room). "Where do you keep the Compact's registry code?" The case, floor to ceiling. The low fever and the nodders. Two nights alone: the grammatical tell (every power attaches to *classified* practitioners) and the box *where does the code say what the word is?* Oona's new tag; "Is it because of me?" / "No"; she will be in the gallery. Wray at the rail before the council: she stands by her words ("Find what it's proudest of"). **War council of six:** "We cannot win this on the merits"; the negotiated withdrawal named and not recommended; "This is your enrollment, not mine to trade"; the third way; "At fifteen."; "Systems have architecture. Architecture has seams."; Naveth will be slow to notice. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:15:| 44 | Enactment Order | 4,697 | Division of labour: Cael and Prynn take the code; Karis takes the founding shelves, for truth not argument; Brom takes witnesses of fact, uncoached; Naveth and Quenna take procedure and lawful delay; Lira: "Not a lawyer wearing your face." Prynn's method: enactment order; "Every amendment is a confession" (the taxonomy master had it from her). The declaration tree, and her dusty laugh. Karis on the steps. Lira at dusk: "You stand like a clerk at a high desk." Log: "New opponent. Four hundred pages, no tells, no third exchange." Letter to Hesk ("Please don't come"). The archive rules; the history of flinching; the schedule almost unscarred. Thu: three of three, then Lira's clap. He flinches and does not light ("One thing, not two"; boxed). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:16:| 45 | The Wrong Road | 5,554 | Day 3: the provision's history; the first draft as a kindness, with Oona's face in it; eleven hours crossed out; "Stop studying my own position. Study his." Prynn: "It's a good road. It's only the wrong one." Day 4: the four-layer structure; the **definitions clause (P15)**; the schedule is the ground. Days 4–6: the schedule read three times; the five places a category can live, each cleared; three refusals recorded; his word absent everywhere; custom in law's coat. Prynn's sixty-years line (verbatim); "I get to say it myself." Karis's report at supper: old registers were sentences and not boxes, and nobody like him yet. **Brom's gauntlet** (day 7, ~2,000 words) follows. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:17:| 46 | At His Own Election | 6,057 | Brom's witness interviews:<br>• Edran: "won't say what he thought it was."<br>• Hobb: "Same as last time. Four times."<br>• Gerda: the entry procedure.<br>• Oona: refused ("I won't call anybody who loves him." / "I don't love him. I study him." / "That's how it starts.").<br>• The aide was asking about *the observer made fire*.<br>Day 8: Lira's maintenance drill, "The argument needs the arguer," and the D6 decision argued on the frozen ring (why show it; "Spend it on purpose"; three, not four). Quenna told before ("the other half of it"). **D6 under Coss's observation** (~1,700 words; see §5). Supper: the story is dead; Edran, "Three of three"; Oona's slate, *I SAW THE FIRST ONE.* The outline (no fallback); the four files (three end; the fourth's eleven words copied, unquoted). Karis begins reading the schedule from the beginning in the evenings. Log, ending "It leaves them later. On whoever loses." |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:20:Brom's gauntlet (ch45) runs as follows:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:21:- **Wray's design:** "I can't fetch you a Silver… I'm going to build one. Out of four people who aren't." No queue; each force starts before the last is finished, and each redirect has to land in the next striker's line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:22:  - Hobb's weight, from the front;
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:23:  - Edran's shell burst, from the west;
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:24:  - Karis's channel shove under his feet;
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:29:  - Round 3: Brom names the wait ("I'm waiting there… And I'm late anyway").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:30:  - The opponents learn: Karis stacks her channel's shove onto Hobb's weight, Edran bursts early, and Lira times into the start of the wait.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:31:- **Wray:** "Not closed… Nobody on this hill can."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:32:- **Brom's column:** *LIRA IN AT THE LAST, THREE OF FOUR.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:41:  - Thu: three of three; Quenna, "You're pale."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:42:  - Fri: Oona's mother arrives by coach and stays in the draper's room over the shop.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:43:  - Sat: Oona's Kindling at the second bell; Lira at the top of the hill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:49:  - Mon/Tue nights: the archive, the tell. Tue evening: Oona's tag.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:50:  - Wed (registry day 1): Wray early; war council; division; Prynn's method; dusk drill; log; Hesk letter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:54:  - Sun–Mon (days 5–6): the schedule read twice more; Prynn's line; Karis's supper report.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:56:  - Mon–Tue: Brom's witness interviews.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:58:  - Wed (day 8): Lira; the D6 decision; Quenna told.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:60:  - Fri–Sat (days 10–11): the outline; Karis starts the schedule (Sat evening).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:65:- **Left forearm burn** (from wk16): itching by Tuesday wk17, which Wray calls the good sign. Kept in a loose sleeve and never used through wk20; still tender.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:71:- **Right shoulder:** the Reydan complaint, unchanged.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:80:  - **Not-doing:** he held it ready and chose not to, at rest; it also did not fire on a fright (Lira's clap). Both are boxed *not yet* and are not an answer to Quenna's question.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:81:- **Karis's rewordings.** One given: "a spark… everything after the spark belongs to whatever you struck it on." She says plainly that she has no second word yet. No "decision point".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:89:  - Panel: Quenna; Wray; the rotating seat by rota, the broad-faced woman from the movement floor (D2's). The heat-Paths instructor is rotated off.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:92:  - "Does the candidate elect to demonstrate anything further?" (first time asked). Cael named the size, the contact, three times, and the rest. Hobb fetched the section-four post and Wray the sand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:94:  - Wray: "Ignition at contact, three of three, at the stated size. No safety concerns."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:95:  - **Quenna (P17):** "The candidate demonstrated, at his own election, an ignition-point capability, contact-adjacent, single channel. Three times, at a size stated in advance, with a rest between. Consistent, observable practice. No safety violation noted. Assessment satisfied."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:96:  - Coss stopped writing at the post, wrote one more line, and asked Quenna only: "Entered as of today's date, Assessor?" / "As of today's date, Warden."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:108:  He knows Coss is lodging in the room over the draper's. He does not know Coss read Oona's notation.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:112:  - Oona's notation as an exhibit of purpose;
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:116:- **Karis:**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:120:- **Oona:** saw D6 from the near bench; is no longer on the observer track; Anchor, Copper; studies him "with permission"; refused as a witness.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:121:- **Wray:** stands by her seven, six and twelve words.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:125:- Brom will call nobody who loves Cael.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:126:- Prynn leaves the door open and sets the tea, and laughed once; she certified the provision forty times and knew the road went nowhere.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:127:- Naveth refused the withdrawal and will be "remarkably slow to notice".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:128:- Quenna: "the other half of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:129:- Edran will testify to fact only.

