editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:23:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:25:- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** by carter; "Six went in. Six came out." beside Gault's last note. Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:27:- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets cut to the uprights' heights); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:30:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:40:- Daeva and Reydan: one log line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:41:- Cash: 102 after the birthday. Brom's string restriction expires on day 100. The crossbow is back on his belt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:25:- **The council, the second honest collision:** Lira for walking away (the fence at forty and the walk at fifty, and pace the third circle on their own time); Brom ("Three hundred's a number a man doesn't reach for." — his father and the horse); Karis ("I would go alone."); **Seln: "Take it… People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face."** Cael's sentence to the whole table (protected), then why: the assumption is wrong and cannot be known to be wrong. **Brom quotes Rooke**, the first person he has ever quoted: "Doors open both ways… I don't like it. I'm in." Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away." The log (EXC-B7-002). Pike marks HOLD unasked and says it to the room. **Teague at the door** (protected): "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted.", the first *Noted* to anyone above them on the wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty meters**: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Anchor let off at ten meters as perception, then as a hand: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30:- **Out at dark:** "There. Back… The clock started again." The bolt-head cut and the shaft drawn; an hour on Brom; a quarter on Lira ("It held a stair…"). His bill: the suite spent on a week's rest. **Seln breaks a stock across the stone**: "No faces." The log (protected). **Teague's crew at full dark** (protected exchange); he does not ask how.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:31:- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:48:Day 115, at the stone in full sun. The kit is on Brom's good shoulder and his bad one is mended once. Lira's arm is closed again with the sling higher. The ledger is in Seln's coat; twenty-nine sheets and forty-one kinds. A brass edge lies on a map. A dead man's last word was *bearing*. "We're going to go look."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:17:It is the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line, the morning after the ferry's last run. Snow is on Lowmarch, the river is skinning with ice, and the ferryman is taking his ropes in. There are five at the lower inn. Lira's arm is slung and her ankle taped, by Oryn's order. Brom's shoulder is bound. Karis has fifty-two sheets, the kit and its ledger, and a map with four circles and a line through them. Seln has the case. Cael is nineteen, with ten fragments and a still place he does not touch. Hesk's straightedge is in his coat and there are 96 marks in hand. Teague's crew is across the yard at the upper inn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:25:- **The fence at the axe-head hold** (~140th, ~3,000 for the set piece). This is two days out on the winter road. A shale-back herd shelters on the fence line's slope and must be moved without stampeding, with no Path that matters. Lira is benched in her sling and reads the herd for them. Brom reads the line of posts like a wall. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. The factor pays forty at the gate and asks no name: 116, and the tenth line, PAID.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:26:- **The ice road** (161st, ~3,000). A carter's cart goes through the river ice. Cael, Brom and Seln haul it out without declaring. Cael's Iron read on the ice's load is the workhorse, taught as a practical skill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:36:**Development:** about 14 Cael beats. Supporting: Lira 2–3, Karis 2–3, Brom 2, Seln 1–2, Oryn 2, Teague 1, Pike 1, the young one 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:49:How many chapters the winter takes, and which log entries become scenes. The shape of the herd problem and the ice rescue. The content of the silent-yard bouts and who wins each. The texture of the inns, the board room, the ferryman's shed, and the long dark. Letters gone west, with answers pending (none arrive in this movement). Humour: Pike's ledger speech; Brom's "It's a boot"; the mule's shed fee "he has not asked for and will".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈82 per 10k (discharge, declaration, Iron Skin as a shout, the lattice point, the seal restated). ≈15 growth beats. Supporting beats for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Pike, the steading's woman, the bowman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:23:- **The ford walked at noon** (sill, slime, the gravel bar thirty by eight, pools that fall away, the near and far shingle). Brom finds his stone with a lip. Lira runs the bar. Seln lies in the grass for two hours. **The lore:** "Dusk. Never noon."; "River's their colour."; "It's because you die." The second man must read as having got *his hand between the jaws and his throat*, not as self-harm (Reader Standard).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:25:- **The ford at dusk, ≈5,000, a learning fight:** the point; the river stands up on three sides; the pommel struck; every head but one. Brom declares Iron Skin, every head turns, he drops it like a coat, "He was still large," and the current takes the hound's hindquarters. Lira runs without a burst and is fast; the ankle goes all the way on the gravel; "I'm fine." **The pack learns** and stops testing silent bodies. Karis holds the knife by its blade with both hands rather than light a second point. **The seam:** they follow the first mover, not a leader, and the grey at the bar's tip is waiting. **One Wind burst, spent openly**, downstream and away from Karis: the landing lock with a dog in it. Seln rises out of the pool behind the grey. Five dead; **two gone downstream, logged as open.** Give the opponent its learning, and keep each decisive exchange in physical terms.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:26:- **Costs on the page:** Brom's forearm open to the bone, wrist to mid-arm; Lira's right ankle, bound flat; Karis's palms cut to the meat, unable to hold a pen; Cael's calf bitten through, in and out, felt only when the water went cold. "Four… Out of five." The bowman: "none of you shouted." **The seal log** (protected; the only restatement). Pike's line by carter; "First honest number…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:27:- **Thornwater, days 54–58:** the calf in elevens; the ladder inventory each morning; Brom carrying nothing for the first time Cael can remember; Karis's barn-table library (three boxes made into shelves with no wall) — "everything I know about the wrong country"; **the cart-yard** (the man with the clouded eye who does not talk roads to paper; the carter's wife: "Everybody knows the quiet ground. Nobody goes in."; *everybody knows* underlined twice; "Not a good one. The first."). The grain moves.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:28:- **The road down:** the steading's woman's last word ("They stop inside, where the tiers are"); camp above the wash; Brom's cloth dark again at the wrist; **Lira at the fire**: Norhold, the ladder, "So what am I becoming, exactly, if nobody's measuring?" Nobody answers it. Cael does not either, because the same fact is his relief and her want.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:29:- **Lowmarch, day 60:** fourteen slips. Seln reads the board and takes the well: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." **Brom at the plank's end:** "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / "Same as anyone… What'd he do?" He writes it on an old slip and keeps it against his skin, the second time in his life (Rooke was the first). Pike: "Held a dog with a shoulder and a river, that one." **The mail** sorted aloud. Hesk's letter (protected), and the grandmother he did not know about. The log. **The saying** at the book, the sheet rewritten by hand: twelfth. "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:30:- **New on the page, days 61–69, the well on the south road.** Seln walks it first and says nothing. A small physical job with a real, mundane hazard (your choice: bad air, a stuck windlass, a fouled shaft; no monster). Four marks. Lira leans the stick against the inn wall on day 64 and walks off. Her first runs on an ankle that bends "less, and later"; fast still, with no one counting. Brom's wrist closes clean on day 66; he looks at it with the lock face and wraps it again. The money is honest (48 → 52 by the movement's end).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:42:The fight's micro-geometry within the planted terrain; how the seam is seen; the barn table's details; which carter says what; the well's hazard; Lira's runs; the humor (Lira on the cart's tail announcing it was her decision; Brom's two-word sentences; Karis made to dictate). Where the Lira and Karis windows sit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:17:It is the 270th day at Lowmarch. There are six now, with Oryn's spring stop at Pike's plank. Lira has two arms she does not quite trust, and Brom's shoulder is still bound and unread. The ferryman says the ice will go in a week, and has said so for a week. Karis's case is made and no one has answered it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:24:- **The week before the ferry** (270th–276th). Tents return to the meadow. Oryn's patients come to the plank, seen from outside. Teague's crew gets ready for spring.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:28:- **The long table** (midday). The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, verbatim; these are their first words to each other. Vastin says the short thing: he resigned or walked out. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence ("Under every station on the continent. I said so at a table in the autumn"). Vastin's new fact: "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail ends at Treswick. Vastin then has nothing to do. Lira asks "Why us." Oryn notices the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that crosses the Line, and the Stair's rim "is not mine". Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only, "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks. **Close (verbatim).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:38:**Development:** about 12 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Karis 2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1, Lira 2, Oryn 1, Pike 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:52:What the week's tents and patients look like. How the landing in flood goes. What Teague's crew does about the stranger. The order of who sits down at the long table, though Lira sits last. How the back room's lamp moves. The texture of Vastin's coat, stick and knee. Humour at the edges: Brom's pricing, Pike's ledger, the mule's empty chair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:16:The Stair's rim on the 115th, with a bearing taken off two sites with a brass edge. Brom's shoulder is mended once, and Lira's arm is closed again. Six people and two mules. Teague's crew is turning back toward Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:23:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and seventy meters. **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:27:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The winter fence** given over ("Ours."). Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "Spring." **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:41:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:51:Book 8 Ch1: Lowmarch with the ice coming and the ferry's ropes taken in. Ninety-six in hand. A kit on a table. A map with a line going off its edge. A healer at Thornwater with a route and an arm to release. A captain's spring term. A fourth circle twice the size behind a fence of iron. And a question asked once at a table that nobody answered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:21:This is the archive's first week. Karis has found the room she has wanted all her life. A marshal learns his name is a blade with no handle. A craftsman shows how he reads a made thing's bones. Brom is offered the life his family wanted and picks up a box. Seln looks at the door his old trade would have used and decides nothing. Then the faction reaches inside the walls. A man with nothing behind him holds a line for people the Compact would restrict, and Cael comes away with the eleventh. We cross the first third into the middle, and progression language surfaces at the turning points: Rune explained, Iron Wall paid, the notice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:32:- **Brom's yard (~2,000).** He rights a broker's cart with his back and no Path, spending the good shoulder. The broker offers a guard's post, a pass and a bed inside the second wall. "I'll think on it." He picks up the box on the bound shoulder, a debt Cael enters. On the stair: "You think Karis is right?" … "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:35:- **The alley (290th dusk; ~4,000, developed).** Staging follows BOOK_MAP §8. Vastin turns uphill and roots the cut wall to wall: "there is no round." Nobody declares. Brom with a loose step-stone. Lira's drop, the knife into the stave's shaft. Cael stands still at the plane's foot for a minute and some, as "the reason". Seln's weighted cord from the roof takes the signaller. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave: none taken, no faces, nobody dead.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:36:- **Costs and the acquisition.** Karis's left hand is cut on a step's edge. Brom binds it with thread, a strip of shirt and his teeth, because no healer inside the gate would put hands on it. Vastin is spent past the road and the knee goes again. **The Iron-Wall notice renders, verbatim.** "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered" / "It's entered." **Not told.** The faction's limit is entered as a finding. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:38:**Physical challenge:** the alley (a major fight) and Brom's cart.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:40:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Brom 2, Seln 2, Karis 2, Cleon 2, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:53:The galleries' geography. The order of the chamber days, and which small discoveries Karis makes on which day. Brom's yard and the broker's words. How the alley's minute feels from two feet below a plane. Where the humour sits: the lamp, the chairs with and without cushions, Brom's "Cart was heavier".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:22:- **Six days Oxhollow → Lowmarch (days 84–90), lightly on the page:** the ford walked quiet a day behind Teague's crew; Lira's carter's boot for two marks, packed with linen; the tape hated by noon; Brom keeps the healer's week to the hour and picks up the middle box with both hands on the eighth morning. A small physical problem on the road is optional and the author's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24:- **The board's room:** the wall rewritten, tenth; "Teague's nine up… He read that slip yesterday. Read it twice… I'd have done the same, and I told him, and he said he knew." **The council, once, in order:** Karis's case; Brom ("A survey kit's a cart's worth… That's not the reason. That's what it is."); Lira ("I'm saying it's a walk and a carry. I'm not saying it isn't the other thing."); Cael: "It pays."; **Seln reads the paper, not the words**: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside." / "It goes in." / "That's not a reason not to go." **The ninety-third**: nobody says *bring her*, and Karis writes "Thornwater, ninety-third. The healer." The Part-1 summary log (protected, "Twelve weeks").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:25:- **Day 91:** marked at the plank in front of eleven witnesses. The mail: **Ephram** and **Vell** (texts protected). **The void road (day 92):** the registry's printed sheet against the ground (seven dashed roads ending in white; this is the third); Karis's carter's map with three blank circles; "Their map has no roads. His has no quiet ground. Between them you get the country." Ephram's letter read at the wash at noon (Bracken told the registry "the Line and nothing past it"; Lira: "Good."). Vell's read at noon on the 94th, aloud, to Lira ("She puts the thing that decides it last." / "So does Ephram.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:27:- **Days 94–95, six on the Fallow road** (Oryn on the mule's down-slope side; the registry sheet goes back into the box at the east gate; past Thornwater's fork the printed sheet is white). **The rise:** he looks at the dark place where an Arbiter would be. Lira's hand up: "It's like the air got thick." Brom: "Like a door closing behind me." Oryn's hands half-raised and silent. Karis: "My Arbiter's gone." Seln: "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Five *backs* at one stride. The stone. **Cael felt nothing, either way, and says nothing**, for two reasons: he doesn't know what it means, and nobody asked. The log at the stone (protected). Camp on the road, no fire. The floor takes the last light like water, and Oryn holds her hands over the line until it's gone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:28:- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A winter either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:29:- **The trials at the stone:** Lira's full burst becomes a step ("It's in me. It's not in the air."; the clock line); Brom's "Skin."; Karis sees every point and can fill none ("It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend."); Seln vanishes for a breath without his Path ("It was never most of what I do."); **Oryn's three crossings** with Brom's arm in her hands ("Nothing in my hands" / "A healer's hands stop working there."). **Cael's two private tests:** the Iron read released before the stride, running across it; at twenty strides a foot's worth of Wind evasion round a stone. From behind it is a man stepping. "It was dark before. It's dark now." Both halves true; together not the truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:30:- **Six over; the site catalogued** (eleven uprights broken at eleven heights; floor twenty-six strides; level under the cord; seamless under his palms, written only as "no seam"; the lip; Karis's chips don't match; the bands "None I own…"). **No instruments anywhere.** **The den** under the far lip (fresh prints; bones in one clause; scat; a hollow worn smooth). "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." Everyone looks at the line and the sun, then at Oryn, then at him. The log at the far lip (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:37:- Oryn reads nobody inside. She has now crossed (with Brom and with the six); her eight solo crossings are M5's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:47:Day 96, the sun on the ridge and going: six people a hundred and forty meters inside a perfect circle, at the far lip of a den. The middle box is on Brom's back and the healer's hands don't work. The stone is two hundred meters west. One of them has told nobody that nothing happened to him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:25:- **The road east (295th–297th; ~5,000).** On the bridge he counts five piers, and does not look at the crown. The spring, with the wind in their faces this time. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited:** "Here." Vastin puts his weight on the knee with the stick off the ground, once. "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted" (Cael's). The feeling of being *known* is entered under each date.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The healers exchange one look, then both look at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more."); it is his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn restates her terms: three holds owed, and "a stop on my own route". "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient, "May I?"** The readings: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced"); Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:35:**Development:** about 14 Cael beats. Supporting: Karis 2, Oryn 2, Vastin 2, Teague 2, Lira 1, Brom 1, the young one 1, Pike 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:13:The morning after the procedure night. Fourteen days to answer. Karis has promised a perfect filing in four days; Brom carries volumes twice a day; Lira keeps the intake away from the records-hall door. Early autumn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:26:- **Brom's two envelopes**: *outcome anticipated*; the Velmere seal two days on the table, the lamp moved; then "the face of a man being offered his whole ledger back." Nobody asks (Lira's rule).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:27:- **Karis spends her budget** (the Greyvane signatures, due before midwinter) and trains the assistant ("find it"). **Ephram and Brom at the frames**, measuring.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:42:The drafting days' shape; the third-year's style beyond Force-builder doctrine; Brom's room and the envelopes; the wool exchange and the market street; the side door's officer; how much of the counsel's coach read survives; warmth at the residence table. The Brom–Ephram frames scene is wordless; keep it that way.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:11:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈82 per 10k (the book's teaching peak: the board, the hold, the nine as held things, tiers at the plank). ≈14 protagonist growth beats. Supporting beats for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Pike, the carter, Teague.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:24:- **C1 (default unless the owner rules otherwise):** in Lowmarch's first week the horse and cart are sold. A horse is fodder and a sign that says *paper*; the scrub ruts past Lowmarch take mules. The sale and what is left of the Book 6 purse become a sealed reserve that Brom's rule keeps them from living on. The log's "in hand" counts only what the board pays. Give it one good scene and an argument with a joke in it, then let it go.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:26:- **Three contracts as short episodes.** The ferry escort (day 14; six crossings; two marks; standing where they can be seen, a job he has done before "at a higher price and for worse people"). The fence-line at the steading (days 22–24; Brom cuts six hours; Karis is asked not to light, does not ask why, and writes down the not-asking; "Cheap"). The wash (day 33; rope; Lira on the far bank, Brom on the near; three wheels; "You're not paper" / "I am"). The ferry broker may carry the hook-and-bar mark, as a plant only. Nothing about him is implied.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:27:- **The hold as a learning arc.** Lira trying runs that end with nothing (a burst is a shout); Brom carrying a load and not hardening; Karis keeping one point she will not light; Cael cataloguing the nine as things *held*, each with its rent: Shadow drifting at dusk (twice, on a road with nobody on it), Anchor wanting every doorway since the Ostrand road, Storm sitting heavy. **No fragment is used in this movement.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: none" through day 49.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:28:- **The Thornwater road (days 41–43), ≈4,000:** the carter at the fire ("Two carts went quiet on it last month"); the stretch at dusk after a wheel cost an hour; positions; the valley's noise; **Lira's hand up at a hole in the noise**; Seln without turning, "Don't declare anything." / "Walk. Same pace."; "I could clear it." / "No." / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it."; Brom becoming exactly as large as his body and no larger; Karis deciding five times not to take out the notebook; the five items (keeps station at forty meters; makes no sound; tracks the buckle; won't cross the gravel fan; reacts to nothing because they gave it nothing); it stops a hundred meters short of the fence. No blow struck.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:30:- **Lowmarch, day 49 — the board anatomized:** a woman captain's line read before and after; the eleven-bale captain ("Say it again and I'll write it"); "The book's for me. The saying's for them."; the wall at the lower inn; "A Bronze who lost my carter…"; "Did you ever hear of a ledger-keeper called Vell?" / "No."; Seln's finger on the carter's map, the asset-restriction **said once and put away**, the map turned east. "Four lines. Nobody lost, nobody hurt, nobody knows you." Brom: "Eleven."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:32:- **Teague across the sill:** he counts his three before the room. He reads Lira from her feet, Brom as a fact, Karis with the beginning of a smile, and Seln on the second pass. Cael reads him back, item by item. Neither speaks. The last of the day lies across the sheet: one word at the top, five names at the bottom, eleven lines of light between.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:45:Chapter boundaries; how much of the skip stays in log-voice; the meadow's life (tents turning over, the ash and the carter with two mules); the three contracts' small problems; the courier's face; Pike's ink-pot and stone; how Seln's window walks a road; the humor (Lira and the board, Brom and animals, Karis underlining). Which scene the C1 sale lands in.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:22:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at four meters.** Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides** (circle and Oryn only). The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and twenty meters, back west. Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at two meters.** Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:23:- **The hour's mending at the line by lantern:** "There. Back." (she does not mention the clock). The state, said because a thing not said is not a finding. **The order (protected, exact)** and the sling; "One arm. From here to the snow."; "The ankle's a tape and a season…"; Oryn flat on the road. Karis's written lines. Seln: "Nothing." Brom: "Hand." / "Morning. Wash it. I've nothing tonight." The log, including **the Book 9 plant line, exactly.** Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes." / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:- **The camp at the stone (night of the 96th → dawn of the 98th):** the unfiled entry (protected). Morning arithmetic aloud: Karis's throat ("Days. Hoarse before it's anything."); Brom's hand ("String… That's two."); **Cael's calf read and not mended**, the fourth failure ("I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."). Oryn against the stake: "Three in two days… That's a route." The route's far end, eleven days north. **Seln at the stake**: the charcoal circle from memory lies on the carter's circle; "Ignorance doesn't stamp iron."; "The Compact knows what quiet ground does. And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." (once); "No… I carried the maps. I never saw the file." Karis: *Where*, then *Entered as said*, then *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* **The contract re-read:** a question, not a recovery; "We just told them."; "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six." The dead hound dragged off and the bolt cut out (five in the sleeve); rations in sixths; nobody says *yours*. Second-night log. **Dawn of the 98th: Oryn's eight crossings alone.** He watches and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:26:- **The loft council, without her:** the conditions as he built them (sustained; stakes on both sides; earnest, on him and not against him); Karis's torn sentence (protected); the price; Lira: "Then tell her. Tonight. Before."; his argument, and its honest underside ("the real one is that I don't know what she'd say"); Seln's "nearest thing to it… I'd enter both."; Brom's "What's it cost her?". **The covenant written before** (protected, whole).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:20:- **The cache, in order**: reclassification orders clipped to Kindling records (forty; "nine weeks of nothing"; **the river-town father's letter and the clerk's honest four-line answer**); field reports (corrected down, never up); two centuries of memoranda (*corrective classification at Kindling evaluation*; Brom: "That's a form."); the leaf in its sleeve (*advisory corrections function*). Seln's four movements; **the finding said once**; "How many?" / "I stopped estimating."; Lira on what being pleasant cost him; "My mother's ledger was always right."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:24:- **Anchor practice, perception only** (new, ~1,500): the private floor; Karis's ignitions as thresholds; Brom holding the door; what the lattice-sense reads in an ordinary room; nothing deployed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:31:- **Reach of the secret: exactly six** (Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin). Not filed, published or used.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:24:- **The slip:** "Ours" (Karis), then "Ours" (Brom). Pike writes a sixth line for the healer. Vastin follows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:26:- **The cut (279th, ~3,500–4,000, developed).** Scout it from the lip first. The factor: "Carters declare, on the ice." Positions as in BOOK_MAP §8. **Iron Wall first shown:** a plane across the road, wall to wall. It holds eight hounds at a run, but the man holding it is rooted and becomes the loudest thing in the cut. Brom works its south end silent with a rock. Lira works the scree with two arms. Cael bursts *away*, then goes still on the scree while the lock beat lands. The pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap; Seln in the heap; the runnel; steel. Five dead and three into the sink ("clear because it's empty, not because it's safe"). Costs: Brom's foot. **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson, verbatim, and the log, verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:27:- **The spring (280th).** Three readers. The instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size; "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin has three reflexes: a directive, a classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. **Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael.** Cael does the sum: his Kindling day, five years and a hundred-some days back. He does not write it, and puts the sheet back. Then: "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." This is the first thing Seln has ever taught anyone. **Close, verbatim:** Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:32:**Cutaway (~1,800):** Seln at the spring. He does the sum and decides to set the sheet in front of Cael without a word. He weighs what it costs to give a thing without saying it. He does not theorize about the deep layer. **The cache stays unopened and undecided.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:33:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Seln 2, Oryn 2, Karis 2, Brom 1, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:46:The drill's details and Vastin's mistakes in it. Exactly how the pack moves on ice. How long the scouting takes. The spring's light and wind. The order in which the three readers find things. How Oryn prices each of them, and the fork's last fire. Whether Vastin's three reflexes come in one scene or across the halt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:17:It is the 291st day. After the alley the working party goes by the carts' street in daylight, with the boxes on a borrowed handcart. Karis's left hand is bound in a strip of Brom's shirt. Cael has eleven fragments and the eleventh has nothing to do. The clerk has not asked three things.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:29:- **The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. Cael gives **Lira the page to read first**; nobody explains it to her. "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom prices it. Seln will keep the cache "a while longer". Karis says two pages, then sleeps on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, taken on his feet and not catalogued, verbatim. "I want to stand in the middle of it." Cleon leaves: "Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:33:**Development:** about 16 Cael beats (the middle-third bump). Supporting: Lira 2, Karis 2, Cleon 2, Vastin 2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1, Oryn 1.
