editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:98:**Who knows the mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln. Nobody else. Oryn becomes the sixth on day 100.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:117:- **Karis's three boxes** (left, middle, right; the middle with a corner worn white). They hold the field archive, the registry's printed continental sheet, the masonry chips (registry-era, standardization-era, pre-standardization, founding-era) and **the Ternhall straightedge** (brass, folding).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:121:- **No weapons of note** beyond knives, Brom's bill-hook and Lira's long knife. **No crossbow** until Oryn hands hers to Brom at the Ring's stone (day 96).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:150:- **The found family's grammar on new terrain** (B6 Ch24): Brom load-balances; Karis indexes; Lira maps; Seln walks every approach first and now says what he finds; Cael catalogues and keeps the log. Watches: two of four hours, never Seln and Brom on the same one.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:154:- **Daeva:** the rematch "relocated," with one log line in this book. **Reydan:** "find me later," one log line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈78 per 10k (Tide taught in full; the herd's derived sense; tiers). ≈17 growth beats. Supporting beats for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Teague, Pike.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16:The seventieth morning, at the plank. The calf is a leg on the flat and says nine uphill. Brom's wrist is closed and must not pull. Lira's ankle is taped and stiff. Karis's palms are two pink lines each. Fifty-two in hand. Teague's crew is out on two hold slips.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:23:- **The fan and the bench, given room (≈7,000):** a cart hauled on a rope; the shelf pitched like a roof; the gorge that gives every sound back late. Lira runs in hundreds; Karis's cord, width and pitch, stones dropped and counted; Brom says a cart on scree "floats" and walks against the strap; Seln is always already where they will sleep. Cael is paid by the line for the first time in his life. **Holding still applies:** he uses nothing on the mountain.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:25:- **The narrowings** and the eighth's clean break. Brom takes the cart across it, and the tail-board doesn't bang because nobody lets it. The ledge in sight. "I'll run it at first light."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:26:- **The ledge and the stampede (≈4,500, terrain fight):** the ledge goes under Lira; her own Wind, full, crosses the gorge; thirty heads come up; the shelf cannot hold them at a run, and they come down the face in a front. "There. Thirty seconds. Lee side." "Cart's gone." **Karis's lattice line** across the face is a declaration the size of a road. The herd splits round the fin at eleven paces; she sits down at the eighth second, emptied. Brom goes back for two boxes (the wrist goes under the cloth). Cael goes after the third. Compression and Anchor *want*, and he prices both and holds, because the split stands on Karis's line and one more loud thing turns it. He takes the shoulder raw: three ribs, left side, low; the calf opened on the shale. The cart floats and goes in with its shafts up. Lira's leg broken under a plate, the boot gone. "That was me… The loud thing." / "It was the ledge. The ledge went. Then it was you." / "Then it was me."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:28:- **Day 80, Oryn**, introduced through her walk and then her hands: "Who's worst?"; the set ("That's the part you'll mind"); the mend in less than an hour (Lira: "Cold… No. It's going along."); she sits as a carter sets down a known load; "That's one."; "Hands on. That's the only way it works… And I can't do it to me."; Brom's wrist ("Then it should have closed in a month and hasn't, because you've pulled on it."); Karis: "Ember. And nothing. You're empty."; "Hm." at the lattice line. **The first failed surface reading** on Cael: she stops in the middle, looks at her hands, tries again, and her face does the instrument's thing. The protected exchange ends on "That's a *finding*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:29:- **Day 81 onward:** tape, explained ("It tells the ribs where the edge is"); the lip, thirty-one paces; **four days down** with her walk catalogued (carter's pace; the down-slope side of the mule; the raw heel taped, because she can't heal herself). **Field care taught** (Lira learns to tape her own ankle properly; Brom learns what a wrapped wrist allows). **The ankle refused** on the arithmetic: "That's a tape and a season." **The route told** at the second night's fire: seven, twenty days, thirty-odd rounds, late eleven times and now twelve, what each owes and what she owes; "That's what late is. It's not a number. It's who I don't know about."; "I remember who I've had my hands on… That's the book."; the city's list by tier; the want (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:44:The bench's days and weather; the herd's look and sound; the exact choreography inside the planted geometry (fin, split, cart, boxes); Oryn's first look at each of them; the walk down; the yard at Oxhollow; which patients come to the table; Lira's and Oryn's windows; humor (Brom's "Carrying." / "Not pulling."; Lira on a mule not mentioning the mule).
