editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:36:- **At the line (dusk).** Every sigil goes dark at the same stride. Lira: "Right." Brom prices the stump. Karis: "It's the first one." Seln gives the count. Vastin: "This is where they drew it." Oryn steps in one stride and back: "Nothing. Everything, round it. Same as you." It goes unanswered. Teague steps in one stride and back: "Field's mine. This isn't field." The turning begins. **The fixed exchange, then "Wait here."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:39:- **The ledger, the letter and the dawn (307th night–308th), verbatim.** Teague: "Next spring … My crew comes." Oryn: "The day I have to." … "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say." "Six. Six and no mule." Vastin is unadmitted. "West." **Closing prose, verbatim.**
