editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-02.md:157:He said it lightly, but Cael had seen the corner of Dace's desk through the door of the little room where the door money was counted. On it, under a lump of slag from the old foundry that served as a paperweight, there was a letter on thick cream paper with a printed head. It was the third such letter Cael had seen there in a year. He had never seen one answered. He had seen one used, on a wet evening in the spring, to light the lamp over the north benches when the spills ran out.
